  "issue_title": "fix(ledger): align cost-ledger hash chain between writer and verifier",
  "issue_body": "## Problem\n\n`scripts/cost_report.py --ledger` always fails hash-chain verification on ledgers\nwritten by `OpenRouterPool._ledger_append` when `TRINITY_COST_LEDGER` is set.\n\nThe writer hashes a compact payload in fixed key order::\n\n    {\"m\":\"<model>\",\"p\":<prompt_tok>,\"c\":<completion_tok>}\n\n`verify_ledger_chain` recomputes the hash with `json.dumps(r, sort_keys=True)`,\nwhich produces a different string (alphabetical key order + spaces). Every\nlegitimate entry is reported as tampered and `cost_report.py` exits with code 2.\n\n`scripts/pack_submission.py::_estimate_cost` has the same mismatch: it never\nadvances `prev_hash` on real entries, so chain integrity is silently skipped.\n\nRelated: #6 (open PR uses a different approach \u2014 this issue centralizes the\n**compact writer format** as canonical).\n\n## Proposed fix\n\n1. Add `src/trinity/llm/cost_ledger.py` as the single source of truth for\n   payload formatting, chained hashing, verification, and safe parsing.\n2. Route `_ledger_append`, `cost_report.verify_ledger_chain`, and\n   `pack_submission._estimate_cost` through the shared module.\n3. Add comprehensive offline tests in `tests/test_cost_ledger.py`.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- [ ] Multi-entry ledger written by `_ledger_append` passes `verify_ledger_chain`\n- [ ] Tampered token counts / missing `h` / broken links are rejected\n- [ ] `pytest tests/test_cost_ledger.py` passes offline\n- [ ] `pack_submission` cost estimate uses verified chain totals\n\n## Impact\n\nTraining receipts and submission packing depend on trustworthy ledger totals.\nWithout this fix, maintainers cannot verify spend and pack_submission silently\nskips chain validation.\n",
  "merged_at": "2026-07-10T14:47:38.000Z",
  "test_cmd": [
